{
	"info": {
		"name": "Hotel Reservation API - Complete Test Suite",
		"description": "Complete testing collection for Hotel Reservation system\n\n**IMPORTANT:** \n1. First run 'Login' to get your Bearer token\n2. The token is automatically saved to {{accessToken}} variable\n3. All requests use this token automatically\n\n**Test Flow:**\n1. Login → Get Token\n2. Create Reservation → Get Location URL + Reservation ID\n3. Get Reservation by ID → Verify creation\n4. Initiate Payment → Complete payment within 10 minutes\n\nCreated for: Junior Developer Training 🎓",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Authentication",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login - Get Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// 📝 LESSON: This script automatically saves your token!",
									"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    ",
									"    // Extract token from response",
									"    if (jsonData.data && jsonData.data.token) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', jsonData.data.token);",
									"        console.log('✅ Token saved successfully!');",
									"        console.log('Token: ' + jsonData.data.token.substring(0, 20) + '...');",
									"    }",
									"}",
									"",
									"// Test assertions",
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response has token', function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data.token).to.be.a('string');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"YourPassword123!\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"description": "🔐 **STEP 1: Login First!**\n\n**What this does:**\n- Authenticates your user\n- Returns a JWT token\n- Automatically saves token to {{accessToken}}\n\n**How to use:**\n1. Replace email/password with your test credentials\n2. Click Send\n3. Check 'Test Results' tab - should say token saved\n4. Now you can use other endpoints!\n\n**For Teachers:** This demonstrates automatic token management using Postman scripts"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Authentication endpoints - Start here!"
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Reservations",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Create Reservation (with LinkGenerator)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// 📝 LESSON: Save the reservation ID for next requests",
									"if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    ",
									"    if (jsonData.data && jsonData.data.id) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('lastReservationId', jsonData.data.id);",
									"        console.log('✅ Reservation created: ' + jsonData.data.id);",
									"        console.log('💳 Payment URL: ' + jsonData.data.paymentUrl);",
									"    }",
									"    ",
									"    // Check Location header (REST best practice)",
									"    var locationHeader = pm.response.headers.get('Location');",
									"    if (locationHeader) {",
									"        console.log('📍 Location header: ' + locationHeader);",
									"    }",
									"}",
									"",
									"// Test assertions",
									"pm.test('Status code is 201 Created', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains Location header', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.header('Location');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response has reservation ID', function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data.id).to.be.a('string');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response has payment URL', function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data.paymentUrl).to.include('/api/Payment/initiate');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"roomId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\n  \"customerId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\n  \"checkInDate\": \"2024-12-25T14:00:00Z\",\n  \"checkOutDate\": \"2024-12-28T11:00:00Z\",\n  \"totalPrice\": 450.00\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Reservation",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Reservation"
							]
						},
						"description": "🎯 **Create a New Reservation**\n\n**What happens:**\n1. ✅ Validates room availability\n2. ✅ Creates pending reservation\n3. ✅ Marks room as unavailable\n4. ✅ Schedules auto-cancellation (10 minutes)\n5. ✅ Returns 201 Created status\n6. ✅ Includes Location header with URL to new resource\n7. ✅ Provides payment URL\n\n**Expected Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"guid\",\n    \"roomNumber\": \"101\",\n    \"status\": \"Pending\",\n    \"expiresAt\": \"2024-01-20T10:10:00Z\",\n    \"paymentUrl\": \"http://localhost:5000/api/Payment/initiate?reservationId=guid\"\n  },\n  \"isSuccess\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Reservation created successfully!\"\n}\n```\n\n**Location Header:**\n```\nLocation: http://localhost:5000/api/Reservation/{id}\n```\n\n**Important for Junior Devs:**\n- 201 Created = Resource successfully created\n- Location header = Where to find the new resource (REST standard)\n- PaymentUrl = Next step in the workflow\n- ExpiresAt = You have 10 minutes to pay!\n\n**Before Running:**\n1. Replace roomId with a valid room GUID from your database\n2. Replace customerId with your customer GUID\n3. Set future dates for check-in/check-out\n4. Make sure room is available!"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Reservation by ID",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Reservation data is returned', function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.isSuccess).to.be.true;",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('id');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('status');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Reservation/{{lastReservationId}}",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Reservation",
								"{{lastReservationId}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "🔍 **Get Reservation Details**\n\n**What this demonstrates:**\n- This is the endpoint that LinkGenerator points to!\n- The Location header from Create Reservation contains this URL\n- RESTful GET by ID pattern\n\n**This automatically uses:**\n- The ID from the previous Create Reservation request\n- Stored in {{lastReservationId}} variable\n\n**You can also:**\n- Paste any reservation ID manually in the URL\n- Test the Location URL from the Create response\n\n**Expected Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"guid\",\n    \"roomId\": \"guid\",\n    \"roomNumber\": \"101\",\n    \"customerId\": \"guid\",\n    \"customerName\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"checkInDate\": \"2024-12-25T14:00:00Z\",\n    \"checkOutDate\": \"2024-12-28T11:00:00Z\",\n    \"totalPrice\": 450.00,\n    \"reservationStatusId\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"Pending\",\n    \"expiresAt\": \"2024-01-20T10:10:00Z\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2024-01-20T10:00:00Z\"\n  },\n  \"isSuccess\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Success\"\n}\n```"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Reservation management endpoints - Create and retrieve reservations"
		},
		{
			"name": "3. Payment",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Initiate Payment for Reservation",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    if (jsonData.data && jsonData.data.paymentId) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('lastPaymentId', jsonData.data.paymentId);",
									"        console.log('💳 Payment initiated: ' + jsonData.data.paymentId);",
									"    }",
									"}",
									"",
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Payment initiated successfully', function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.isSuccess).to.be.true;",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"reservationId\": \"{{lastReservationId}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Payment/initiate",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Payment",
								"initiate"
							]
						},
						"description": "💳 **Start Payment Process**\n\n**Workflow:**\n1. Create Reservation (you get payment URL)\n2. **Use this endpoint** to start payment\n3. Complete payment with Stripe\n4. Verify payment\n\n**This uses:**\n- {{lastReservationId}} from previous Create Reservation\n- Or you can paste any reservation ID\n\n**Remember:** You have 10 minutes from reservation creation!"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Payment History",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Payment/history/{{lastReservationId}}",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Payment",
								"history",
								"{{lastReservationId}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "📜 **View all payment attempts for a reservation**\n\nUseful to see:\n- Failed payment attempts\n- Successful payments\n- Payment timestamps\n- Transaction IDs"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Payment-related endpoints"
		},
		{
			"name": "4. Testing Scenarios",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Test: Room Not Available",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"roomId\": \"{{lastReservationId}}\",\n  \"customerId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\",\n  \"checkInDate\": \"2024-12-25T14:00:00Z\",\n  \"checkOutDate\": \"2024-12-28T11:00:00Z\",\n  \"totalPrice\": 450.00\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Reservation",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Reservation"
							]
						},
						"description": "🧪 **Test Scenario: Double Booking Prevention**\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n- Should return 400 Bad Request\n- Error message about room not available\n- No reservation created\n\n**Why test this?**\nEnsures your system prevents double bookings!"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Test: Validation Error",
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{accessToken}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"roomId\": \"invalid-guid\",\n  \"customerId\": \"\",\n  \"checkInDate\": \"2024-12-28T14:00:00Z\",\n  \"checkOutDate\": \"2024-12-25T11:00:00Z\",\n  \"totalPrice\": -50\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Reservation",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"Reservation"
							]
						},
						"description": "🧪 **Test Scenario: Invalid Data**\n\n**This tests:**\n- Invalid GUID format\n- Empty required fields\n- CheckOut before CheckIn\n- Negative price\n\n**Expected:**\n- 400 Bad Request\n- Detailed validation errors\n- ErrorCode: ValidationError"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Test different scenarios and edge cases"
		}
	],
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "baseUrl",
			"value": "https://localhost:7061",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
